{"content":[{"c":["SHECANIAH, SHECHANIAH*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Descendant of David through the line of Zerubbabel living in postexilic Palestine (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.21-22","r":"1Chr.3.21-22","rawR":"1Chr.3.21-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.21-22","value":"1Chr.3.21-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:21-22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Levite and the head of the 10th of 24 divisions of priests formed during the reign of David (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.11","r":"1Chr.24.11","rawR":"1Chr.24.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.11","value":"1Chr.24.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 24:11"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. One of six priests serving under Kore during the reign of King Hezekiah of Judah (715–686 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). Shecaniah assisted with the distribution of the temple offerings among his fellow priests living in the priestly cities (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.31.15","r":"2Chr.31.15","rawR":"2Chr.31.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.31.15","value":"2Chr.31.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 31:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Father of Hattush, who returned with Ezra to Judah following the Babylonian captivity during the reign of King Artaxerxes I of Persia (464–424 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.3","r":"Ezra.8.3","rawR":"Ezra.8.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.3","value":"Ezra.8.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Son of Jahaziel who returned with Ezra to Judah during the reign of King Artaxerxes I of Persia (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.5","r":"Ezra.8.5","rawR":"Ezra.8.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.5","value":"Ezra.8.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Son of Jehiel in the house of Elam, who urged Ezra to command the sons of Israel to divorce the foreign women they had married (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.2","r":"Ezra.10.2","rawR":"Ezra.10.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.2","value":"Ezra.10.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["7. Father of Shemaiah. Shemaiah, the keeper of the East Gate, helped Nehemiah rebuild a section of the Jerusalem wall (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.29","r":"Neh.3.29","rawR":"Neh.3.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.29","value":"Neh.3.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:29"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["8. Father-in-law of Tobiah the Ammonite and the son of Arah (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.6.18","r":"Neh.6.18","rawR":"Neh.6.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.6.18","value":"Neh.6.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 6:18"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["9. Head of a priestly family who returned to Judah with Zerubbabel following the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.3","r":"Neh.12.3","rawR":"Neh.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.3","value":"Neh.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:3"},"). Shecaniah is perhaps identical with Shebaniah in verse ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.14","r":"Neh.12.14","rawR":"Neh.12.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.14","value":"Neh.12.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"14"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Shebaniah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Shebaniah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Shebaniah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Shebaniah #3"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"ShecaniahShechaniah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:21-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.21-22","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.21-22","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.21-22"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 24:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.24.11","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.24.11","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.24.11"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 31:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.31.15","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.31.15","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.31.15"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 8:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.8.3","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.8.3","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.8.3"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 8:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.8.5","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.8.5","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.8.5"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.2","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.2","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.2"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.29","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.29","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.29"},{"anchorText":"Neh 6:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.6.18","rawQueryValue":"Neh.6.18","sourceRefExact":"Neh.6.18"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.3","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.3","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.3"},{"anchorText":"14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.14","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.14","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6cfaae2570558b347069288b746997e22d0cdc7385104b90389448c14a6b41eb","sourceItemName":"ShecaniahShechaniah","sourceItemOrder":245,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"ShecaniahShechaniah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Shecaniah, Shechaniah*","title":"Shecaniah, Shechaniah*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}